<section id="about" class="section about">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>About me</h2>
    <p>
      I'm a software engineer who has spent over a decade shipping iOS and macOS apps,
      with a backend life in Python on the side. I care about building things that are
      genuinely useful, feel great to use, and don't get in the way.
    </p>
    <p>
      These days I'm channelling that into indie making — building my own small,
      focused products that scratch real itches. I use AI to help me move faster and
      reach beyond my comfort zone into new platforms (like this very website).
    </p>
    <p>
      When I'm not coding I'm probably thinking about why the iOS simulator is so
      slow, or reading about someone who quit their job to build a spreadsheet app.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="writing" class="section latest-writing">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading-row">
      <div>
        <h2>Latest writing</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Notes on software, indie apps, and the small decisions behind building useful products.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="section-link" href="/blog/" data-umami-event="View Blog Click">View all posts</a>
    </div>

    {% set latestPosts = collections.posts | limit(3) %}
    {% if latestPosts.length %}
      <div class="blog-list">
        {% for post in latestPosts %}
          <article class="blog-card">
            <p class="post-meta"><time datetime="{{ post.date | htmlDateString }}">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</time></p>
            <h3><a href="{{ post.url }}" data-umami-event="Homepage Post Click">{{ post.data.title }}</a></h3>
            <p class="blog-card-desc">{{ post.data.description }}</p>
            {% if post.data.tags %}
              <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Post tags">
                {% for tag in post.data.tags %}
                  <li><a class="tag" href="{{ tag | tagUrl }}">{{ tag }}</a></li>
                {% endfor %}
              </ul>
            {% endif %}
          </article>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="projects" class="section projects">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Projects</h2>
    <div class="project-grid">

      <article class="project-card">
        <div class="project-header">
          <h3>Reach</h3>
          <span class="platform-badge">iOS</span>
          <img class="app-icon" src="/icons/Reach.png" alt="Reach app icon" />
        </div>
        <p class="project-tagline">Your Audience.</p>
        <p class="project-desc">
          Raising the minimum deployment target in an Xcode project shouldn't be a leap
          of faith. Reach shows you exactly which devices you'd lose and the real-world
          user impact — so you can make an informed call, not a guess.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="project-card">
        <div class="project-header">
          <h3>VoucherVault</h3>
          <span class="platform-badge">iOS</span>
          <img class="app-icon" src="/icons/VoucherVault.png" alt="VoucherVault app icon" />
        </div>
        <p class="project-tagline">Never lose a voucher again.</p>
        <p class="project-desc">
          Your store for screenshots of vouchers and reward cards. Scan barcodes and
          QR codes to keep everything in one tidy place — ready the moment you need
          it at the checkout.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="project-card">
        <div class="project-header">
          <h3>StoryVision</h3>
          <span class="platform-badge">iOS</span>
          <img class="app-icon" src="/icons/StoryVision.png" alt="StoryVision app icon" />
        </div>
        <p class="project-tagline">Turn your words into worlds.</p>
        <p class="project-desc">
          Speak a story out loud, watch it transcribe in real time, then tap once to
          transform it into a stunning AI-generated image. No typing, no friction —
          just imagination and a voice. Perfect for parents, writers, and creators
          who want to see their ideas come alive instantly.
        </p>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
